--TEST--
`Core\Json::decodeAs<T>` over a `tainted string` document is refused where a text property of `T` is written without `tainted`, and the program's own document fills the same class — `rule:security/derived-codec-qualifiers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Note {
    public function constructor(
        public string $title,
    ) {}
}

// The program's own document: a plain property is allowed.
Note $own = Core\Json::decodeAs<Note>("{\"title\":\"own\"}");
echo $own->title, "\n";

// A document from outside the program: `$title` must be `tainted`.
tainted string $outside = "{\"title\":\"x\"}" as tainted string;
Note $note = Core\Json::decodeAs<Note>($outside);
echo $note->title, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0810]: `Note::$title` is declared `string`, and `Core\Json::decodeAs` fills it with text from outside the program
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
